# Keep the working tree LF on every platform.
#
# Biome is configured with `lineEnding: "lf"` (biome.json), so a Windows
# checkout made under git's default `core.autocrlf=true` fails `bun run lint`
# on every tracked file — the contents are correct, only the line endings are
# not. Declaring the repository text-normalized makes the checkout LF
# regardless of the contributor's local autocrlf setting, and is a no-op on
# macOS and Linux, which already check out LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
